"F16773"	"tools/PhotoReview.Benchmark.Cli/RawSurvey.cs"	"752"	"832"	"MethodDeclaration"	"RawSurvey.public static string GenerateMarkdownReport(SurveySummary summary)"	"ISSUE"	"REVIEW-UNNUMBERED: R20 (P2 candidate): SurveyFileAsync marks WIC output as preview-only whenever decoded width/height exactly equals largest embedded JPEG, without requiring a RAW format or comparing the container sensor dimensions. A RAW whose full-size WIC result is same dimensions as its embedded full-size JPEG is therefore misclassified; BuildConclusions then counts it as preview-only and claims WIC is not reliable for full-resolution, and GenerateMarkdownReport labels it Yes (preview). Current test helper can inject previewOnly=false directly; existing tests do not exercise SurveyFileAsync with equal sensor/preview/WIC dimensions and do not validate the derived report label. Compare decoded dimensions with known sensor dimensions/orientation (or use a reliable decode-source signal) and add an end-to-end seam oracle. Static only; no tests/build/runtime."
